    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks, i'll probably just sleep it off lol. but it's still bothering me because even if it's just a draft or a pest, it's so weirdly timed. it's always right when the browning starts—like the moment the pan gets really hot and the smell changes, that's when the \"shadows\" appear or the steam does that weird breathing thing.\n\nit's like the chaos is tied to the cooking itself. is there any chance that certain chemical reactions, like when things start to caramelize or sear really intensely, can actually cause these kinds of visual weirdness or strange \"movements\" through things like rapid gas release or light refraction? or am i just totally losing it?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
